From 18d7c630b6b41c5c42a2d3cd389c1f107f2d368e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:57:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] notifications: optional ntfy Title/Priority/Tags
 headers

Add a `ntfy_headers` config flag (default false). When enabled, the
notification worker sets ntfy's Title, Priority and Tags HTTP headers
derived from the notification type, so an ntfy client renders a titled,
prioritized, tagged notification instead of a bare line:

  Warning    -> Title "Rayhunter alert",          Priority high,    Tags rotating_light,warning
  LowBattery -> Title "Rayhunter: low battery",   Priority default, Tags battery,warning
  Update     -> Title "Rayhunter: update available", Priority low,  Tags arrow_up

When false (the default) the POST body is sent plain, unchanged from
today, which keeps a generic webhook receiver working. A webhook that is
not ntfy simply ignores the extra headers.

Wires the flag through config.toml, the web config form and the config
template, and covers both the enabled and plain paths with tests (the
test server now captures request headers).

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-045.
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
